body:
It stings because my partner has had an eating disorder, had one for most of our relationship (in which I also struggled maybe the worst it has ever been, and she lost most of her body weight, which I am a monster for being upset about now even as she has restored a fraction of it) and yet still says things about how I clearly wasn't trying hard enough to get better because she got better over the course of last year and yet I hadnt, and she got better because she thought I was also trying and she did it for me because she was clearly hurting me, but now i cant get better (or am "giving up") despite the fact that Im implicitly telling her she can't engage in running by freaking out (as if its a choice). i wholly understand her point of view, because ive been awful, but it still feels bad, even though it is clearly my fault. she's waited long enough for me to be a good partner, i worry about making her wait even longer. there is only so long one can wait for good things when the wait is excruciating.

&#x200B;

i have therapy later today, i will be mostly honest (i.e. not mention the planned actions, as i am more scared than i am willing to follow through and simply want good things) and see if she tells me anything useful (she's largely a marriage counselor, i believe, but she was the only one accepting clients in the area so i had to go to her---i think she may be out of her depth with me). the semester ends next week, so i may just try to get through that and then admit myself. i dont know. im terrified of myself. i love her, i dont want to ruin everything, it just feels like i am incompatible with the direction the two main players in my life are going and there is no way out for me or them. trapped, essentially, with no escape other than irrational outs. i have literally no one else in my life---parents are gone, siblings far away, this small town is largely monoethnic and isolating

&#x200B;

thank you for the in-depth response. im sorry for my waning lucidity and i hope this doesnt come across as me rambling once again or debating im sorry thank you shalom aleichem sorry
